            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can stress them. Budget conventional generators often have high THD and voltage swings when motors start, which can upset furnace boards, UPS units and some variable-speed appliances. Most phone chargers and laptops cope fine. Using a conventional model rated under 5 percent THD, or running electronics through a battery or UPS, reduces the risk considerably."
